# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SECRETS — never commit these.
#
# .bridge_secret is the shared secret guarding the OAuth bridge. The bridge
# binds 0.0.0.0 so the agent CONTAINER can reach it, which means without the
# secret any local process can spend the subscription. It is the only thing
# standing between an open port and your account.
#
# NOTE: .bridge_secret and 11 .jwt_secret files are ALREADY TRACKED in history.
# Adding them here stops future commits but does not remove them from past ones.
# See the untracking + rotation steps at the bottom of this file.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.bridge_secret
.jwt_secret
**/.jwt_secret
*.pem
*.key
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
credentials.json
.credentials.json

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Generated by runs. ~2.5 GB combined, and all of it is reproducible.
#
#   jobs/    raw Harbor trials: trajectories, verifier output, collected /app
#   output/  repackage.py's derived tree, rebuilt from jobs/ at any time
#   logs/    bridge and run logs
#
# jobs/ additionally contains .jwt_secret files and whatever the agent wrote,
# so committing it leaks secrets as well as bloating the repo.
#
# Keep delivery/ (the small CSV + HTML summary) if you want results in git.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
jobs/
output/
logs/
*.log
!logs/*.sh

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Python
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local state and scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.omo/
sqlite_mcp_server.db
*.sqlite
*.sqlite3
tasks.zip
*.tar.gz
/tmp/
scratch/
tasks/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Editors / OS
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Deliberately NOT ignored:
#
#   tasks/*/solution/     the reference apps. They are the answer key, and the
#                         corpus rule is that solution/ never reaches an agent,
#                         training data, or a public dataset -- but it belongs
#                         in the private repo, since the oracle gate depends on
#                         it. If this repo is ever made public, that rule needs
#                         a separate answer.
#   bin/                  the launcher scripts
#   environment/          the service catalog
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ===========================================================================
# BEFORE YOUR FIRST PUSH — the tracked secrets must be dealt with:
#
#   git rm --cached .bridge_secret
#   git rm --cached --ignore-unmatch 'jobs/**/.jwt_secret'
#   git rm -r --cached jobs output logs .venv
#   git commit -m "untrack secrets and generated artefacts"
#
# That removes them from the WORKING tree's index, not from history. Anything
# already pushed is still recoverable from earlier commits, so also:
#
#   * rotate .bridge_secret (generate a new value; the old one is compromised)
#   * if this repo has ever been pushed anywhere, treat the old secret as public
#   * to scrub history entirely, use git-filter-repo or BFG before publishing
# ===========================================================================

# Serena (coding-assistant tooling) -- editor-side config, not part of the
# harness. Nothing under bin/, harness/ or environment/ reads it, and
# project.yml carries a per-developer project name.
.serena/

# Generated by environment/providers/test_all_apis.py -- 2.8 MB of captured
# responses and a report, regenerated by running the script. Not an input to
# any task or grader.
environment/providers/api_test_responses.json
environment/providers/api_test_report.md

# Local docs and scratch. Deliberately untracked (2026-08-14): these are working
# notes and per-developer scratch, not harness inputs. Files stay on disk.
.omo/
docs/
SPEC example/
FLOW.md
OVERVIEW.md
PLAN.md
TEAM_GUIDE.md
sqlite_mcp_server.db
